{{ phrase_blacklist(banned_phrases=banned_phrases, title="") }}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Emotional craft: contrast, white space, emotional expression diversity -#}
{% macro emotional_craft_rules(title="### Emotional Craft") %}
{% if title %}{{ title }}{% endif %}
- **Contrast creates emotion**: In high-intensity emotional scenes, use one discordant daily detail, gentle action, or calm observation to amplify emotional impact, rather than stacking same-intensity descriptions. In light scenes, can bury one discordant note to create unease.
- **White space is expression**: At the character's most painful or shocking moments, allow silence, action interruption, topic shift, or environmental blank description to replace direct depiction. Not all emotions need to be named—the emotions readers infer from the character's behavioral choices are more powerful than being told.
- **Emotions do not stack with isomorphism**: In the same scene, use only one expression channel for the same emotion (action/dialogue/body/environment/silence); do not repeat the same channel.
{% endmacro %}